{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Get one of the predefine log streams. This is the quick'n'easy solution to access {\b Assimp}'s log system. Attaching a log stream can slightly reduce {\b Assimp}'s overall import performance.\par
Usage is rather simple (this will stream the log to a file, named log.txt, and the stdout stream of the process: {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid {\cf17 struct }aiLogStream c;\par
c = aiGetPredefinedLogStream(aiDefaultLogStream_FILE,{\cf22 "log.txt"});\par
aiAttachLogStream(&c);\par
c = aiGetPredefinedLogStream(aiDefaultLogStream_STDOUT,NULL);\par
aiAttachLogStream(&c);\par
}
\par
